Terrible game. It uses 44 GB of disk space yet the textures are incredibly blurry, low detailed and stretched, and this is on high settings.
It uses an ancient id tech 5 game engine with a ♥♥♥♥♥♥ MegaTexture technology. This really takes off an depth from the game. It might be ok for a game released in 2004, but not in 2014.
Pros:
- classic FPS;
- dual wield weapons;
- really good sound effects;
- main character voice acting;
- pretty cool music matching action on the screen;
- a sort of stealth system with knife kills;
- a sort of cover system with lean mechanics.
Cons:
- awfully blurry and low detailed textures. I mean really, really low detailed textures;
- poor optimization, stutters in some sections of the map for no reason.
- minimal post-processing effects.
- pretty dumb AI and I play on almost highest difficulty setting;
- pretty boring story;
- very limited game options in UI.
I highly recommend do not buy this game, and if you still wanna try it just make sure you meet Steam's conditions in case of refund.

